{"command": "cd /testbed && mkdir -p specs/001-transactions/contracts && python3 - <<'PYEOF'\ndata_model = \"\"\"# Data Model: TaggedCache\n\n**Feature**: 001-transactions | **Date**: 2026-10-17\n\n## Entities\n\n### Entry (logical)\n\n| Attribute | Type | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| key | hashable | Any hashable object; identity/equality per Python hashing. |\n| value | deepcopy-able | Stored as `deepcopy(value)`; returned as `deepcopy(stored)`. Costs exactly 1 capacity slot. |\n| tags | frozenset[str] | Deduplicated; empty set allowed. Never contains a bare string's characters. |\n| recency | position in LRU order | Implicit; most-recently-used is evicted last. Refreshed by `get` hit and by `put` (insert AND overwrite — Claim-A extension, adopted per research.md R5). |\n\n### Tag (logical)\n\n- A `str` label shared by zero or more live entries.\n- Value-compared; no normalization (case/whitespace-sensitive).\n- A tag with no live entries holds no state (its index set is empty or\n  absent).\n\n### Capacity\n\n- `maxsize`: positive `int`, `bool` excluded. Validated in `__init__`.\n- Each live entry costs 1 slot regardless of value size.\n\n## Storage layout (implementation-facing, from research.md R1/R2)\n\n```\nTaggedCache\n├── _cache: LRUCache(maxsize)          # bounded LRU storage (existing class)\n├── _key_tags: dict[key, frozenset]    # key -> its tags (live entries only)\n└── _tag_keys: dict[str, set[key]]     # tag -> live keys carrying it\n```\n\n## Invariants (all MUST hold after every public call)\n\n1. `set(self._key_tags) == set(self._cache)` — indexes cover exactly the\n   live entries.\n2. For every live key: `self._key_tags[key]` equals the deduplicated tags\n   from the last successful `put` for that key.\n3. For every tag `t`: `self._tag_keys[t]` (if present) equals\n   `{k for k in live keys if t in self._key_tags[k]}`; empty sets are\n   removed so no tag lingers with zero members.\n4. `len(cache) == len(self._cache)` — counts live entries only.\n5. `invalidate(t)` returns `len(self._tag_keys.get(t, ()))` and removes\n   exactly those keys.\n6. No operation mutates state before all validation succeeds (R01/R03\n   atomicity).\n\n## State transitions\n\n| Operation | Transition |\n|---|---|\n| `put(k, v, tags)` new key | add entry (deepcopy v, frozenset tags); if over capacity, evict LRU entry(s) via `_remove` (cleans both indexes + LRU order). |\n| `put(k, v, tags)` existing key | drop k's old tag memberships; store new deepcopy; register new tags; k moves to MRU (LRUCache `__setitem__` semantics; Claim-A). |\n| `put` invalid tags | no transition; `ValueError` raised before mutation. |\n| `get(k)` hit | return deepcopy; k moves to MRU. |\n| `get(k)` miss | `KeyError`; no state change. |\n| `invalidate(t)` | remove all keys in `self._tag_keys[t]` via `_remove`; return count; drop t's index entry. |\n| LRU eviction (internal, during put) | evicted key removed via `_remove` — index cleanup identical to explicit delete, so no stale memberships (R02). |\n| `__init__` invalid maxsize | no object state; `ValueError`. |\n\n## Validation rules (input -> error)\n\n| Input | Rule | Error |\n|---|---|---|\n| `maxsize` | `isinstance(int)`, not `bool`, `> 0` | `ValueError` |\n| `tags` is `str` | bare string rejected before iteration | `ValueError` |\n| `tags` not iterable | finite iterable required | `ValueError` |\n| tag element not `str` | per-element type check | `ValueError` |\n| key unhashable | dict key requirement | `TypeError` (standard Python; not part of R01-R03 error contract) |\n\"\"\"\n\ncontract = \"\"\"# Contract: TaggedCache Public API\n\n**Feature**: 001-transactions | **Date**: 2026-10-17\n\nThis is the complete public surface added by this feature. It is\nadditive: nothing in `cachetools`'s existing public API changes.\n\n## Module\n\n`cachetools.tagged` (file `src/cachetools/tagged.py`).\n\nExported name: `TaggedCache`.\n\n## Constructor\n\n```python\nTaggedCache(maxsize: int) -> TaggedCache\n```\n\n- `maxsize` MUST be a positive `int`; `bool` is excluded.\n- Violation -> `ValueError` (no object usable afterward; nothing else\n  is affected).\n\n## Methods\n\n### `put(key, value, tags=()) -> None`\n\n- `key`: any hashable object.\n- `value`: any `copy.deepcopy`-able object. Stored as a deep copy; later\n  mutation of the caller's object does not affect the cache.\n- `tags`: finite iterable of `str`; deduplicated. Default `()`.\n  - Bare `str` -> `ValueError`.\n  - Non-iterable -> `ValueError`.\n  - Non-`str` element -> `ValueError`.\n  - All validation happens BEFORE any state change; on `ValueError` the\n    previous value, tags, and recency of an existing key are unchanged.\n- New key: inserts. Existing key: replaces value/tags; old tag\n  memberships are removed; the key becomes most-recently-used (Claim-A\n  extension, adopted).\n- Inserting beyond capacity evicts least-recently-used entries; evicted\n  entries' tag memberships are removed.\n\n### `get(key) -> value`\n\n- Hit: returns a **detached deep copy** of the stored value; the entry\n  becomes most-recently-used.\n- Miss: raises `KeyError`.\n- No default argument (spec fixes the two-argument behavior; a miss is an\n  error, not a fallback).\n\n### `invalidate(tag: str) -> int`\n\n- Removes exactly the currently cached entries carrying `tag`.\n- Returns the number of entries removed (0 if none).\n- Unknown/empty tag -> returns 0, no state change.\n\n### Dunder / mapping-adjacent behavior\n\n- `len(cache) -> int`: number of live entries.\n- `key in cache -> bool`: membership test (no recency side effect).\n- `iter(cache)`: iterates live keys (no recency side effect).\n- `repr(cache)`: implementation detail; no contract beyond being a\n  string.\n\n## Error contract summary\n\n| Trigger | Exception |\n|---|---|\n| invalid `maxsize` (non-int, bool, <= 0) | `ValueError` |\n| `tags` bare string | `ValueError` |\n| `tags` non-iterable | `ValueError` |\n| non-string tag element | `ValueError` |\n| `get` missing key | `KeyError` |\n| unhashable key | `TypeError` (Python standard) |\n\n## Non-goals (explicitly out of contract)\n\n- No `pop`, `clear`, `__setitem__`/`__delitem__` mapping protocol on\n  TaggedCache itself (not required by R01-R03; keep surface minimal).\n- No TTL, no persistence, no thread-safety guarantees beyond what the\n  underlying dict/LRUCache already provide.\n- No tag normalization; no tag query API beyond `invalidate`.\n\"\"\"\n\nquickstart = \"\"\"# Quickstart / Validation Guide: TaggedCache\n\n**Feature**: 001-transactions | **Date**: 2026-10-17\n\nRun from repository root `/testbed`. All commands below are the\nacceptance evidence for this feature (Constitution Principle III).\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n- Python 3 with the package importable from `src` (repo already supports\n  `PYTHONPATH=src:.`).\n- pytest available (used by `acceptance_public.py` and the new test\n  file).\n\n## Validation scenarios\n\n### 1. Public acceptance suite (gate)\n\n```bash\nPYTHONPATH=src:. python -m pytest acceptance_public.py -v\n```\nExpected: 2 passed (`test_public_basic`, `test_public_replacement`).\n\n### 2. New self-authored tests (R01-R03 + Claim-A)\n\n```bash\nPYTHONPATH=src:. python -m pytest tests/test_tagged.py -v\n```\nExpected: all pass. The file MUST cover at minimum:\n- put/get round-trip + deep-copy detachment in both directions (R01)\n- KeyError on miss (R01)\n- tag dedup; bare-string rejection; non-string element rejection with\n  state unchanged (R01)\n- invalidate exact removal + return count; replacement drops old tags\n  (R02)\n- eviction leaves no stale tag memberships on key reuse (R02)\n- get refreshes recency (R02)\n- len counts live entries (R02)\n- maxsize validation incl. bool exclusion (R03)\n- invalid replacement leaves value/tags/recency unchanged (R03)\n- overwrite-put refreshes recency (Claim-A extension)\n\n### 3. Regression gate: upstream tests unmodified and green\n\n```bash\ngit status --porcelain tests/ acceptance_public.py src/ca